**(B)** non-conductors

The forbidden energy gap $E_g$ between the valence band and the conduction band is:
- **metals/conductors**: $E_g\approx0$ (bands overlap) — conduction is easy;
- **semiconductors**: $E_g\approx1$ eV (Si 1.1 eV, Ge 0.7 eV) — a modest temperature or field frees carriers;
- **insulators (non-conductors)**: $E_g\gtrsim3$ eV (diamond $\approx5.5$ eV) — practically no carrier is excited at ordinary temperatures.

So the widest forbidden band belongs to the insulators.
